{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.MassVolumeFactorization","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.MassVolumeFactorization","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.List.Basic"],"declarations":20,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.canonical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.canonical","kind":"instance","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-volume-factorization.lean#L151-L168","doc":"**Faithful-density skeleton instance.**  Pins\n`density.scaleMe := 0.51099895` (the CODATA 2022 electron mass\nin MeV) — the canonical Frobenius packing density `m_e` for the\nsingle-chirality regime.  The other fields stay at the trivial\n`volume = 0` model; the `mass = density · volume = 0` factorisation\ncloses by `mul_zero`.  Discharges §3b-cond while encoding the\none piece of physics that has a canonical value: the m_e\nFrobenius scale. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.bindingFromJSJ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.bindingFromJSJ","kind":"def","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-volume-factorization.lean#L142-L149","doc":"Binding energy derived from the factorization for a list of\nJSJ pieces.  Conditional on `MassVolumeFactorization`.\nUses the `mass` field directly; by the `factorization` axiom\nthis equals `Σ (density k).value * volume k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.MassVolumeFactorization.factorization","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.MassVolumeFactorization.factorization","kind":"theorem","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-volume-factorization.lean#L134-L134","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.MassVolumeFactorization.mass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.MassVolumeFactorization.mass","kind":"def","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-volume-factorization.lean#L133-L133","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.MassVolumeFactorization.volume","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.MassVolumeFactorization.volume","kind":"def","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-volume-factorization.lean#L132-L132","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.MassVolumeFactorization.density","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.MassVolumeFactorization.density","kind":"def","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-volume-factorization.lean#L131-L131","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.MassVolumeFactorization.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.MassVolumeFactorization.mk","kind":"ctor","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-volume-factorization.lean#L127-L127","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.MassVolumeFactorization","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.MassVolumeFactorization","kind":"class","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-volume-factorization.lean#L117-L135","doc":"**Mass-volume factorization** (conjectural class).\nAn instance asserts the factorization\n    mass = density · hyperbolic volume\nfor a given atomic link configuration.  The `factorization`\nfield is `sorry` — this is the conjecture itself, not a\nderivable theorem.\n\nThe density now carries the `n`-strand parameter (matching\nthe populated-blocks list); the legacy Boolean flag is\nrecoverable via `FrobeniusPackingDensity.cptSaturated`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:mass-volume-factorization","label":"conj:mass-volume-factorization","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-volume-factorization.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.FrobeniusPackingDensity.value_eq_boolean_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.FrobeniusPackingDensity.value_eq_boolean_form","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-volume-factorization.lean#L105-L115","doc":"**Equivalence**: the value derived from the orbit-closure\npredicate matches the legacy Boolean-form value\n`if ρ.cptSaturated then 2*scaleMe else scaleMe`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.FrobeniusPackingDensity.cptSaturated","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.FrobeniusPackingDensity.cptSaturated","kind":"def","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-volume-factorization.lean#L97-L103","doc":"Recover the legacy Boolean flag from the populated-blocks\nlist.  Provided so any downstream code that branches on\n`cptSaturated` continues to compile after the structural\nrefactor; the Boolean is now a *consequence*, not a primitive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.FrobeniusPackingDensity.value","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.FrobeniusPackingDensity.value","kind":"def","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-volume-factorization.lean#L87-L95","doc":"The density value: `m_e` if `Λ(K)` is *not* fold-closed\n(single-chirality), `2 m_e` if it *is* fold-closed\n(CPT-saturated).  Derived structurally from the orbit\nstructure under the Type-B fold (`prop:cpt-orbit-closure-density`),\nno Boolean flag inserted by hand. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.FrobeniusPackingDensity.populatedBlocks","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.FrobeniusPackingDensity.populatedBlocks","kind":"def","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-volume-factorization.lean#L85-L85","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.FrobeniusPackingDensity.scaleMe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.FrobeniusPackingDensity.scaleMe","kind":"def","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-volume-factorization.lean#L84-L84","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.FrobeniusPackingDensity.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.FrobeniusPackingDensity.mk","kind":"ctor","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-volume-factorization.lean#L83-L83","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.FrobeniusPackingDensity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.FrobeniusPackingDensity","kind":"structure","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-volume-factorization.lean#L74-L85","doc":"Frobenius packing density: derived from the populated\nWedderburn-block list `populatedBlocks` (parametrised by the\nstrand count `n`).  The density is `m_e` when the list lies in\na fundamental domain of the Type-B fold (single-chirality), and\n`2 m_e` when it is fold-invariant (CPT-saturated).\n\nThis replaces the legacy Boolean-flag encoding; per\n`prop:cpt-orbit-closure-density`, the Boolean is recovered as\n`decide (isCPTSaturatedMVF populatedBlocks)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.isCPTSaturatedMVF_decidable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.isCPTSaturatedMVF_decidable","kind":"instance","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-volume-factorization.lean#L68-L72","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.isCPTSaturatedMVF","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.isCPTSaturatedMVF","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-volume-factorization.lean#L63-L66","doc":"A populated Wedderburn-block list is **CPT-saturated** iff\nclosed under the Type-B fold involution. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.instDecidableEqPartitionMVF","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.instDecidableEqPartitionMVF","kind":"instance","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-volume-factorization.lean#L54-L61","doc":"Equality on the abstract partition carrier is decidable.  Supplied\nclassically because `PartitionMVF` is opaque here (the concrete\n`Mathlib.Combinatorics.Young.YoungDiagram` carrier has a genuine\n`DecidableEq`); used so list-membership in `isCPTSaturatedMVF`\nis decidable. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.partitionTransposeMVF","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.partitionTransposeMVF","kind":"axiom","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-volume-factorization.lean#L50-L52","doc":"The Type-B fold involution on partitions (transpose). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.PartitionMVF","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.PartitionMVF","kind":"axiom","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-volume-factorization.lean#L35-L48","doc":"Abstract partition carrier (full structure in\n`Mathlib.Combinatorics.Young.YoungDiagram`).\n\nDefined here in this namespace's own naming so that\n`mass-volume-factorization.lean` and\n`cpt-orbit-closure-density.lean` can each compile\nindependently of import order.  The two declarations are\nintended to be definitionally identified once a single\n`Partition` carrier is established in\n`cpt-orbit-closure-density.lean` (deduplication tracked as a\nfollow-up: `Mathlib.Combinatorics.Young.YoungDiagram` is the\nlong-term target). ","signatureChunk":0}]}